<header><p class="st-kicker">chiefdom · Horn and East Africa</p><h1 class="st-title">Mirambo's state</h1><p class="st-meta">1860 CE – 1884 CE (approx.) · capital Iselamagazi</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">A powerful Nyamwezi state built by the warlord Mirambo, who challenged the Arab traders of Tabora for control of the caravan routes.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mirambo">Mirambo</a>, a Nyamwezi chief's son from the small chiefdom of Uyowa, built a military following in the 1860s from ruga-ruga, armed young men often of captive or uprooted origin. From his capital at Iselamagazi he conquered neighbouring chiefdoms and created a large state known as Urambo, west of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tabora">Tabora</a>.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mirambo">Mirambo's</a> power rested on firearms, ruga-ruga warriors and control of trade. From 1871 to 1875 he fought the Arab and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/swahili">Swahili</a> traders of <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/unyanyembe">Unyanyembe</a>, closing the routes to the lake and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ujiji">Ujiji</a>. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/henry-morton-stanley">Henry Morton Stanley</a>, who met him in 1876, compared him to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/napoleon">Napoleon</a>. He later made peace and dealt with missionaries and the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/sultanate-of-zanzibar">Sultanate of Zanzibar</a>.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mirambo">Mirambo</a> died in 1884, and without his leadership the state fragmented among subordinate chiefs. Its lands passed under <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/german-east-africa">German East Africa</a> within a few years. The town and district of Urambo keep his name.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><div class="st-emblem" role="img" aria-label="chiefdom, 1860 CE – 1884 CE (approx.)"><svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true"><ellipse cx="44" cy="56" rx="16" ry="24"/><path d="M44 34 V78"/><path d="M68 20 V84"/><path d="M68 20 L63 30 H73 Z"/></svg><p class="st-emblem-type">chiefdom</p><p class="st-emblem-region">Horn and East Africa</p><div class="st-span" aria-h